{"id":"orbital-fd975f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Icon generator output fails RuboCop, keeping make test red on main","description":"`orbital/bin/generate-icons` writes an em dash in the file header (`Style/AsciiComments`) and a blank line before the module's closing `end` (`Layout/EmptyLinesAroundModuleBody`).\n\nBoth offences are present on `main` before any dependency change, so `make test` stops at `orbital-lint-ruby`. Autocorrecting `icons.rb` would not last, because the next regeneration brings them back. The fix belongs in the generator.\n\nFound during, and fixed on the branch of, orbital-07708c, which regenerates `icons.rb`.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-fd975f","target_id":"orbital-07708c","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:17:20.027344Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-c8c570","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Evaluate held-back major dependency upgrades","description":"orbital-07708c limited updates to minor and patch versions. These majors were held back.\n\n**Direct dependencies**\n- `puma` 7.2.1 → 8.0.2\n- `solid_cable` 3.0.12 → 4.1.0\n- `brakeman` 7.1.2 → 8.1.0\n- `image_processing` 1.14.0 → 2.2.0\n- `typescript` 5.9.3 → 7.0.2 (needs a `package.json` change)\n- `postcss-cli` 11.0.1 → 12.0.0 (needs a `package.json` change)\n\n**Transitive gems**\n- `bigdecimal` 3.3.1 → 4.1.3\n- `connection_pool` 2.5.5 → 3.0.2\n- `diff-lcs` 1.6.2 → 2.0.0\n- `json` 2.21.2 → 3.1.0\n- `marcel` 1.2.1 → 2.1.0\n- `minitest` 5.27.0 → 6.0.6\n- `net-ssh` 7.3.8 → 8.1.0\n- `parallel` 1.28.0 → 2.3.0\n- `prism` 1.9.0 → 2.1.0\n- `rdoc` 6.17.0 → 8.1.0\n\nSome transitive gems may be capped by what their parent gems allow.\n\nNote that `demo/` has no tests (`bin/rails test` reports 0 runs), so upgrades there need browser checks.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aL","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-c8c570","target_id":"orbital-07708c","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:21:30.966318Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-07708c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f4acb3ab-956e-4587-b00f-9d63271bcf05","text":"**Ready for review.** Nothing is committed yet; changes are in the issue's worktree.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Baseline:** `required_ruby_version \u003e= 3.4.8`, `demo/.ruby-version` and `demo/Dockerfile` at 4.0.9, Rails 8.1.4.1, `orb_template` 0.3.0.\n- **Other dependencies:** all gems and npm packages at their newest minor or patch. Held-back majors are listed in a follow-up BACKLOG issue.\n- **Icons:** `icons.rb` regenerated from Lucide 1.68.0. 306 icons added, none removed.\n- **Lint fixes:** 8 new offences from the RuboCop bump fixed in `menu/item.rb`, `menu/sub.rb`, `modal.rb`, `modal_frame.rb`, `progress_bar.rb`, `text.rb` and `components/attributes.rb`.\n- **Generator fix:** `bin/generate-icons` no longer produces the 2 offences that kept `make test` red on `main` (orbital-fd975f).\n\n## Decisions not in the original spec\n\n- Tracked `orbital/app/assets` bundles were unminified watch builds. `make build` replaces them with minified output (`index.js` drops from 212 kB to 75 kB), which accounts for most of the deletions.\n- Fixed the generator on this branch because this branch regenerates `icons.rb` and `make test` could not pass otherwise.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make build` and `make test` pass on Ruby 4.0.9. `orbital/` RSpec passes on 3.4.8 (20 examples).\n- All 37 demo pages return 200 on 4.0.9. Compared with `main` on the old stack, the rendered HTML differs only in per-request tokens, random IDs and Lucide icon shapes.\n- In the browser: dialog open and close, nav dropdown, select and accordion all work, with no console errors or warnings on the pages where console messages were checked.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- `demo/` has 0 tests, so `bin/rails test` passing says nothing about it.\n- The Docker image was not built, so the `ruby:4.0.9-slim` tag and native gem builds in it are untested.\n- `orbital-menu` and `orbital-menu-sub` submenus, avatar and the popover demo page were rendered but not exercised by click.\n- The compiled CSS change was checked by eye on two pages only (home and dialog)."},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:21:30.98865Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-8aec06","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Adopt security stack from orb_template","description":"Adopt the `make security` stack from `orb_template` (Trivy, `bundle-audit`, Brakeman) and its `test-rubies` target, adapted to this repo's two projects, and run it from `make test`.\n\nBlocked by orbital-07708c: the Trivy gate fails until that issue's npm fixes land.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-8aec06","target_id":"orbital-07708c","kind":"blocked_by"}],"labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:33:18.790412Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-8aec06","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:35:29.924003Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-07708c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b7b1aadf-0d29-42a7-a882-951f2e15bb6f","text":"**Correction and update. Ready for review again.**\n\nThe earlier comment said all npm packages were at their newest minor or patch. That was wrong: `bun update` moved only direct dependencies, leaving known-vulnerable indirect versions locked.\n\n## Change\n\nRegenerated `orbital/bun.lock` and `demo/bun.lock`. `package.json` ranges are unchanged by this step, and no overrides or ignore rules were added. Now locked: `picomatch` 2.3.2 and 4.0.7, `yaml` 2.9.1, `browserslist` 4.29.5, `immutable` 5.1.9.\n\n## Side effects\n\n- **Indirect major bumps in `orbital/bun.lock`:** `@types/node` 24 → 26, `chokidar` 4 → 5, `readdirp` 4 → 5, `undici-types` 7 → 8, and the top-level `picomatch` 2 → 4. These are allowed by their parents' ranges, and tsc passes.\n- **`index.css` is smaller:** 77.31 kB → 71.65 kB when built from the old and new lockfiles. A rule-by-rule comparison shows no `Orbital-*` selectors lost. The optimizer now merges more rules, and browser targets moved to current versions, dropping older ones such as Chrome 112.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Trivy with dev dependencies: 0 vulnerabilities and 0 secrets in both projects. One LOW misconfiguration remains (`DS-0026`, no Dockerfile `HEALTHCHECK`).\n- `bun audit`: no vulnerabilities in either project. `bundle-audit` on `demo/`: none. Brakeman on `demo/`: 0 warnings, though it reported only 3 templates, so it appears to skip `.orb` views.\n- `make build` and `make test` pass on 4.0.9. `orbital/` RSpec passes on 3.4.8 (20 examples). All 37 demo pages return 200.\n- In the browser with the rebuilt bundles: dialog open and close, menu popover and submenu all work, with no console errors.\n\n## Still not verified\n\n- `bundle-audit` has not run against `orbital/Gemfile.lock`, because the gem isn't in that Gemfile yet (orbital-8aec06). Trivy did scan that lockfile.\n- The Docker image has not been built.\n- The select, accordion and nav dropdown were clicked before the lockfile regeneration, not after. Avatar and the popover demo page have not been click-tested.\n- `demo/` has 0 tests."},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:35:38.309119Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
