{"id":"orbital-8aec06","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:53:22.177845Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-8aec06","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3b1b473e-ea64-44ab-8f93-8b2dc8e4c75e","text":"**Ready for review.** Nothing is committed yet; changes are in the issue's worktree.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **`trivy.yaml`:** based on `orb_template`'s, with dev dependencies included and repo-specific skip dirs.\n- **`Makefile`:** new `security`, `trivy`, `audit`, `bun-audit`, `brakeman` and `test-rubies` targets. `make test` now runs `security`.\n- **`orbital/Gemfile`:** adds `bundler-audit`. The lockfile gains only that gem.\n\n## Decisions not in the original spec\n\n- `make brakeman` runs twice: on `demo/`, and on the gem with `--force`, from the demo bundle.\n- `bun audit` uses `--audit-level=high` to match the Trivy gate. Moderate npm findings don't fail the build and `bun audit` doesn't print them. Trivy's report-only pass still lists them, except nested `bun.lock` entries, which Trivy doesn't report.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Planted issue | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `make trivy` | `picomatch` 2.3.1 as a dev dependency | fails |\n| `make bun-audit` | `picomatch` 2.3.1 as a dev dependency | fails |\n| `make security` | `picomatch` 2.3.1 as a dev dependency | fails |\n| `make brakeman` | command injection in a gem component | fails |\n| `bundle-audit` directly | pre-update `demo/Gemfile.lock` (245 advisories) | fails |\n| `make bun-audit`, `make trivy` | `yaml` 2.8.1 (moderate only) | passes, as intended |\n| `make test-rubies` | Ruby not installed (`RUBIES=9.9.9`) | fails with a clear message |\n\nOn the clean tree, `make security`, `make test` and `make test-rubies` (3.4.8 and 4.0.9) all pass. The only finding reported is the LOW `DS-0026`.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- **Brakeman does not parse `.orb`.** A planted `raw(params[...])` was caught in `.erb` and missed in `.orb`. It also missed one in a component class. A clean Brakeman result does not cover XSS in the views or components, and this is recorded in the `Makefile`.\n- `make test` now needs `trivy` installed and network access.\n- `make audit` itself wasn't run against a vulnerable lockfile; `bundle-audit` was tested directly with the same check."},"created_at":"2026-11-04T20:56:10.905212Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
