{"id":"orbital-3877b6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Components render raw ORB source unless the app also requires orb_template","description":"`lib/orbital.rb` requires `view_component` but never `orb_template`. `Bundler.require` only loads gems listed directly in an app's Gemfile, so an app that lists only `orbital` never loads ORB, and components using `orb_template` output their template source as text.\n\n**Reproduce:** in a new Rails app with only `gem \"orbital\", github: \"kuyio/orbital\", tag: \"v0.2.0\"`, render `Orbital::Badge`. The output is `\u003cspan **html_attributes\u003e {{render_icon}} ...`.\n\n**Measured with the 37 top-level components, each rendered with no arguments:**\n- `orbital` only: 9 fine, 26 raw, 2 raised.\n- `orbital` plus `gem \"orb_template\"`: 29 fine, 0 raw, 8 raised. The raised ones were not investigated; they may just need required arguments.\n\n**Why nothing caught it:** the root `Gemfile` lists `orb_template`, so the docs site loads it. The test suite covers only Grid and InlineStack and doesn't check for raw template output.\n\nThe bug predates the move to the repo root: the `lib/orbital.rb` at `980ae51` has the same requires.\n\n**Fix:** require `orb_template` from `lib/orbital.rb`, and add a test that boots with only the gem's own requires and renders an ORB component.\n\n**Workaround:** add `gem \"orb_template\"` to the app's Gemfile.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aN","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-3877b6","target_id":"orbital-8b131a","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T09:33:49.266326Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
