{"id":"orbital-e1b2e4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Six components raise NameError unless the app adds Orbital to ORB.namespaces","description":"Orbital's own templates use bare component tags such as `\u003cIcon\u003e` and `\u003cModal\u003e`, which ORB resolves through `ORB.namespaces`. The gem never adds itself to that list. The docs site does, in `test/dummy/config/initializers/orb.rb`, which hides the problem.\n\n**Reproduce:** in a new Rails app listing only `orbital`, render `Orbital::Spinner`. It raises `uninitialized constant Orbital::Spinner::Icon`.\n\n**Affected:** Alert, CheckBox, Dialog, Dropdown, Select and Spinner.\n\n**Measured at `a69c19e`, with all 37 top-level components rendered with no arguments:**\n- No namespace configured: 29 fine, 8 raised.\n- `ORB.namespaces = %w[Orbital]`: 35 fine, 2 raised. Those two, Icon and Image, correctly report a missing required attribute.\n\n**Fix options:**\n- Have the gem add `Orbital` to the list. An app that assigns `ORB.namespaces = [...]` afterwards would overwrite it.\n- Qualify the tags in the gem's own templates, so they don't depend on app configuration. This looks more robust and needs checking against how ORB resolves qualified names.\n\nAdd a test covering these six components, with no namespace configured by the test setup.\n\n**Workaround:** `ORB.namespaces += %w[Orbital]` in an initializer.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aN","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-e1b2e4","target_id":"orbital-3877b6","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T09:40:38.773695Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-3877b6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-59432761-5f79-49d3-a5bf-48665dd92f93","text":"**Check before tagging:** a new app listing only `orbital` from GitHub at `a69c19e` had no components rendering raw source: 29 fine, 0 raw, 8 raised. Two of the 8 correctly report a missing required attribute. The other 6 are a separate bug in how the gem's own templates resolve component names, filed as `orbital-1` follow-up below.\n\n**`v0.2.1` was not tagged** because of that bug, so the README on `main` names a tag that doesn't exist yet."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T09:40:40.720318Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-3877b6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0d2597bf-4c84-4d61-a7ae-6fafabd0769a","text":"**Correction to the comment above:** the separate bug is `orbital-e1b2e4`."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T09:40:43.747382Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
