{"id":"orbital-33ae5a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-be95cd8c-8ca2-49eb-8e72-a90873f1875e","text":"**Summary:** `Card` accepts `gap` and `padding`, applied to `.Orbital-Card-Content` through `data-gap` and `data-padding`. A Card with neither renders the same HTML as before. The docs page has two new examples and a props table, and `test/components/orbital_ui/card_test.rb` covers the attributes.\n\n**Decision not in the issue:** the markup uses a splat rather than bound attributes, because a bound attribute on an HTML tag renders nil as `data-gap=\"\"`, which would match the `[data-gap]` selector.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:14:12.038972Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
