{"id":"orbital-bbc141","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Test that every component and slot renders","description":"The tests cover only a handful of components, so bugs like raw template output and missing namespaces reached a release candidate. Add a suite that finds every component from `app/components`, renders it, and renders each of its slots, and that fails when a new component or slot isn't covered. Requested by the maintainer.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:17:25.438795Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-bbc141","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:17:34.800243Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-bbc141","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:17:35.067008Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-e2394d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"CheckBox emits invalid \u003c/input\u003e, and Expander ignores vertical and class","description":"Found by the render suite in `orbital-bbc141`.\n\n- **CheckBox:** `\u003cinput **html_attributes /\u003e` goes through `content_tag`, which renders `\u003cinput ...\u003e\u003c/input\u003e`. A void element can't have an end tag, so this is invalid HTML, though browsers ignore it.\n- **Expander:** the template hardcodes `\u003cdiv class=\"Orbital-Expander\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e` and never uses `html_attributes`. `vertical`, `class` and any other attributes are silently dropped, so the documented `\u003cExpander vertical/\u003e` never gets `.Orbital-Expander--vertical`.\n\nFixed in the same change as `orbital-bbc141`.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-e2394d","target_id":"orbital-bbc141","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:18:54.5299Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-bbc141","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-aa74c0d5-03e8-4581-997a-4a0ef290b615","text":"**Summary:** `test/components/orbital_ui/every_component_test.rb` generates a render test for all 48 components found under `app/components` and for every slot, including each type of a polymorphic slot. Each render must be non-empty, well-formed HTML with no raw template syntax. `test_helper.rb` now sets `ORB.namespaces` as the README requires.\n\n**Found and fixed:** `orbital-e2394d`, in `CheckBox` and `Expander`.\n\n**Verified by reintroducing bugs:** removing the `orb_template` require, the namespace setup, the Expander or CheckBox fix, Image's `src`, or Card's splat each makes the suite fail, as does breaking a template.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:20:48.455417Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-5b6a71","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Popcard ignores position and on, because redefined attributes are processed twice","description":"Found while tracing `method redefined` warnings in `orbital-bbc141`.\n\n`attribute_definitions` copies the parent's definitions, and `attribute` appends, so a subclass that redefines an attribute holds two definitions of it. `initialize` loops over both. The first pass consumes the caller's value with `kwargs.delete`, and the second finds nothing and resets the attribute to the default.\n\n**Effect:** `Popcard.new(position: :s, on: :click)` ends up with `position: :n, on: :hover`. `Popcard` is the only affected component today, because it is the only subclass that redefines attributes.\n\n**Fix:** `attribute` replaces an inherited definition of the same name.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a2","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-5b6a71","target_id":"orbital-bbc141","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:22:34.19726Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-5b6a71","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-95d29168-32ae-4a0c-aa4a-112b5e6d74ba","text":"**Summary:** `attribute` now replaces an inherited definition of the same name, so `Popcard` keeps the `position` and `on` it's given. Tests cover the caller's value, the subclass default, the parent staying unchanged, and no component holding duplicate definitions. Fixed in the same change as `orbital-bbc141`.\n\n**Verified:** with the fix removed, the suite fails. The docs page's `\u003cPopcard position=\"s\"\u003e` and `\u003cPopcard on=\"click\"\u003e` now render those values.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:23:53.052436Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-bbc141","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1461b98e-5519-4d03-b787-71b65ba6d39d","text":"**Warnings:** the `method redefined` warnings traced to a real bug, `orbital-5b6a71`. `test_helper.rb` now turns any Ruby warning from this gem's own code into a failure, and sets `load_defaults` so the Rails 7.1 run has no deprecation warning. `make test`, `make test-rubies` and the Rails 7.1 run produce no warnings."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:23:54.650372Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
