{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Make Orbital work cleanly alongside an app's own Tailwind v4","description":"Testing an app with its own Tailwind v4 next to the gem's CSS found gaps a new user would hit:\n\n- `Expander`'s CSS is outside any cascade layer, so app utilities can't override it.\n- `dark:` utilities follow the OS setting, while Orbital switches on a `.dark` class.\n- `@import \"orbital_ui/theme\"`, as documented, probably doesn't resolve from an installed gem.\n- The README doesn't describe the setup, including that theme overrides must stay outside `@layer`.\n\nRequested by the maintainer.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:35:03.934839Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:35:29.49126Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:35:29.741648Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3f3c32dc-0f35-477e-b38e-b76381aeddbb","text":"**Summary:** `Expander`'s CSS is now in the components layer. `theme.css` makes `dark:` follow the `.dark` class. `app/assets/tailwind/orbital_ui/engine.css` lets `tailwindcss-rails` apps import the theme, and the README has a \"Using with Tailwind\" section.\n\n**Decision not in the spec:** the README tells apps to link `\"tailwind\"` by name, because `stylesheet_link_tag :app` also links the generated engine file, whose absolute `@import` fails in the browser with a 404.\n\n**Tested end to end:** a real Rails 8.1 app with Propshaft and `tailwindcss-rails` 4.7.0, in a browser, and a Node build importing from the `v0.3.1` tag on GitHub.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:38:05.574318Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:41:48.52533Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-71a7e733-f79e-4978-b035-c582c93a78c1","text":"**Revision:** replaced the `tailwindcss-rails` engine approach with `bin/rails generate orbital_ui:install`, as the maintainer preferred. It sets up `ORB.namespaces`, the layout tags and the Tailwind theme, and running it again changes nothing. `engine.css` is removed. The spec is updated.\n\n**Tested end to end:** a new Rails 8.1 app with Propshaft and `tailwindcss-rails`, using the built gem's contents, with the generator as the only setup step, checked in a browser.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:44:36.790791Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:54:38.168059Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Make Orbital work with rails new -j bun -c tailwind and -c sass","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-11-06T10:54:38.77925Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-abfab4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"TextField drops unknown attributes, and multiline ignores its value","description":"Found while building a real app in `orbital-62f832`.\n\n- `TextField` never uses `html_attributes`, so `id`, `class`, `data-*`, `aria-*`, `min`, `step`, `maxlength` and any other attribute are silently dropped. An app can't attach a Stimulus action to an input, set a number field's range, or target it by id.\n- With `multiline`, `value` is rendered as an attribute on `\u003ctextarea\u003e`, which browsers ignore, so an existing value never displays.\n\n**Fix:** build the input from `html_attributes`, as `CheckBox` does, and render a textarea's value as its content.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-abfab4","target_id":"orbital-62f832","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:03:38.1485Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:05:38.056777Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-abfab4","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f7af45c0-072a-4616-be3d-0572511843e2","text":"**Summary:** `TextField` now builds its input from `html_attributes`, so unknown attributes reach the input, and a given `id` is used for the input and its label. A `multiline` field renders its value as content. `test/components/orbital_ui/text_field_test.rb` covers both. Fixed in the same change as `orbital-62f832`.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:05:38.07781Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e0dd38e0-511d-4312-a996-fefa511b6509","text":"**Revision:** the generator now targets `app/assets/stylesheets/application.tailwind.css`, the path `rails new -c tailwind` creates. `tailwindcss-rails` is dropped everywhere. The generator also adds a `dialogs` frame and replaces `stylesheet_link_tag :app` in Tailwind apps. The docs no longer claim Orbital only styles its components.\n\n**Proof:** a fictional finance app built only with the documented steps and Orbital components, run under `bin/dev`, and exercised in a browser. Building it found `orbital-abfab4` and the Accordion and placeholder fixes in this change.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:05:38.099811Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-4ca9ca","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Tooltip's inner wrapper breaks percentage sizing of its content","description":"`Tooltip` wraps its content in `\u003cdiv data-orbital-popover-target=\"trigger\"\u003e`, which has no classes and can't be styled through the component. A `class` passed to `Tooltip` goes on the outer element only, so a child sized with a percentage, such as a chart bar with `height: 91%`, collapses to 0 by 0.\n\n**Found while** building a real app in `orbital-62f832`. It needed this workaround:\n\n```orb\n\u003cTooltip class=\"h-full flex-1 [\u0026\u003ediv:first-child]:flex [\u0026\u003ediv:first-child]:h-full [\u0026\u003ediv:first-child]:items-end\"\u003e\n```\n\n**To decide:** make the wrapper `display: contents`, or give it a way to fill its parent, or attach the trigger behaviour to the outer element and remove the wrapper. Check the positioning code, since the popover is anchored to the trigger target.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aL","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-4ca9ca","target_id":"orbital-62f832","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:10:26.917295Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-8a965f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Make Grid columns responsive","description":"`Grid` takes a single `columns` value, so a layout can't change its column count by screen size. A typical dashboard needs one column on a phone and four on a desktop.\n\n**Found while** building a real app in `orbital-62f832`, which used Tailwind's `grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4` instead of `Grid`.\n\n**To decide:** the API, for example `columns={{sm: 2, lg: 4}}`. There is already an `OrbitalUi::Type::Breakpoints` attribute type to look at. Shipped CSS is compiled, so the values need rules in `grid.css`, or a custom property approach.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aM","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-8a965f","target_id":"orbital-62f832","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:10:30.221051Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-0de15d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"NavigationMenu has no header wrapper or padding of its own","description":"`NavigationMenu` has no padding, so used on its own it sits against the window edges and clips whatever is at the far right, such as an avatar. The docs site gets its spacing from `Demo::AppFrame`'s `Page` wrapper, which isn't part of the gem, so a new app has nothing to copy.\n\n**Found while** building a real app in `orbital-62f832`, which added its own wrapper:\n\n```html\n\u003cheader class=\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b bg-background/90 px-4 py-2 backdrop-blur\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl\"\u003e...\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/header\u003e\n```\n\n**To decide:** give it sensible default padding, add props such as `sticky` and `bordered`, or ship a page or header component. At the least, the docs page should show a complete header.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aN","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-0de15d","target_id":"orbital-62f832","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:10:33.91836Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-eb84b2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"NavigationMenu has no way to keep controls visible when collapsed","description":"When `NavigationMenu` collapses on a narrow screen, everything except the brand and the hamburger button is hidden, including controls that apps usually keep visible, such as a theme toggle or account menu. An app can only repeat them inside the `Mobile` slot's menu.\n\n**Found while** building a real app in `orbital-62f832`, where the theme toggle and account menu disappeared on narrow screens.\n\n**To decide:** add a slot for controls that stay visible at every width, such as `\u003cNavigationMenu:Actions\u003e`.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aO","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-eb84b2","target_id":"orbital-62f832","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:10:36.726403Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-89e408","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Number input arrows stay light in dark mode","description":"In dark mode, the browser's up and down arrows on `\u003cTextField type=\"number\"\u003e` stay white, which stands out against the dark input.\n\n**Found while** building a real app in `orbital-62f832`, in its transfer dialog.\n\n**Likely fix:** set `color-scheme: dark` under `.dark` and `color-scheme: light` under `:root` in `theme.css`, so browser-drawn controls follow the theme. That also affects scrollbars, date pickers and other native controls, so check those in both themes.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aP","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-89e408","target_id":"orbital-62f832","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:10:39.268903Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-8c907e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-cacc158c-baa1-4c9d-819a-ab0abffa256c","text":"A real app built in `orbital-62f832` needed this: its transaction list was the largest piece of plain HTML on the page. Things the component should handle, based on that table:\n\n- A row target for client-side filtering, so attributes such as `data-table-search-target=\"row\"` reach the `\u003ctr\u003e`.\n- Hiding columns at narrow widths, as `hidden md:table-cell` did there.\n- A flush layout inside a `Card` with `padding=\"0\"`, lining up with the card header's 24px padding.\n- Right-aligned amount columns, and a narrow actions column for a row `Dropdown`.\n- An empty state for when no rows match.\n\nI'd do this before the other new components."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:10:42.202992Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-62f832","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"walkthrough","filename":"walkthrough.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:15:49.348133Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-abfab4","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-57e93e9b-3726-4779-870c-f180c5c0f9bd","text":"Merged as part of `orbital-62f832`, whose walkthrough covers it. The change: `TextField#default_attributes` now holds the input's attributes, and `render_input` builds from `html_attributes`, the same pattern as `CheckBox`. `id` became a declared attribute so the label and input share it."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:15:50.696622Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
