{"id":"orbital-8a7c72","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:42:39.514486Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-8a7c72","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7cedc5ba-2822-45a9-8661-3425e7a10ef4","text":"**Summary:** Added `OrbitalUi::Form` and `OrbitalUi::Form::Builder`, with CSS, a docs page and tests. `\u003cForm:TextField name=\"email\"/\u003e` gets its name, id, value, label and error from the model. `Select` accepts `value` and matches integers. `Form:CheckBox` follows the model and sends a hidden `0`. Fernhill now has a `Transfer` model with validations.\n\n**Verified in a browser:** invalid transfers show errors inside the dialog, with the page untouched and values kept. A valid one closes the dialog and updates the page, through `turbo_stream.refresh`. Fields render inside a `Grid`, tested.\n\n**Decisions:** see the spec: Rails' `field_name` and `field_id`, and no global `field_error_proc` override.\n\n**Status:** ready for review; not committed."},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:47:02.996195Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
