{"id":"orbital-92be63","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Docs code panels show HTML entities inside expressions","description":"The docs site's code panels double-escape some source. For example, `SampleAccount.new(name: \"Sam Taylor\")` displays as `SampleAccount.new(name: \u0026quot;Sam Taylor\u0026quot;)`, and `\u0026:validate` displays as `\u0026amp;:validate`, so a copied example is broken.\n\n**Found on:** `/components/select` (132 occurrences), `/components/form` (13), `/themes` (6), `/blocks` (2) and `/components/dialog` (2).\n\n**Likely source:** `highlight_line` in `test/dummy/app/components/demo/code_block.rb`, not yet confirmed. It only affects the docs site, and doesn't ship in the gem.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aQ","dependencies":[{"source_id":"orbital-92be63","target_id":"orbital-8a7c72","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-11-06T11:51:36.84882Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.318 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
